Observations (backlog, not grounds for FAIL):
 O1 Cleanup's `chmod -R u+rwX "$TMP"` (unchanged from attempt 3) does change out's mode, but only to delete
    the temp dir, after keep-or-drop. Item 4's "never changed" holds for the judgment, not for deletion.
 O2 The poll loop forks /usr/bin/sleep 5 times a second for the whole Codex run (<=9000 forks at the
    1800 s default). This is negligible, but it is a cost the bare wait did not have.
 O3 Test hygiene: "U A4-2 an ABSOLUTE manifest path" builds its path under $WORK. Under a long TMPDIR
    (>200 bytes) the old regex already rejects it by length, so that test alone does not discriminate
    there. The /etc/hostname case does.
 O4 Shell semantics for probe writers: a harness started as a simple background command from a
    non-interactive shell (`setsid cmd &`) inherits SIGINT as ignored, and bash cannot trap it. The
    oracle's `( exec setsid ... ) &` form is correct. This is not a harness defect.
